{
  "description": "A compatibility-preserving diagnostic adapter for Self-EvolveRec that measures the trained recommender and supplies an interpretation prompt grounded in measured metrics and their definitions. It supports architecture changes while retaining the four-dataset RecHarness evaluation protocol.",
  "motivation": "Guide model improvements using observable training behavior and public interaction data, while preventing unsupported claims about reviews, ratings, or latent user traits.",
  "implementation_notes": "Retain DiagnosisProbe(view, device), run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), and diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis). Return metrics and metric_definitions. Inspect view.model as the actual trained module; adapt embedding, sequence-feature, and scoring probes to its architecture. Consume batches shaped (None, sequence, positive, negative), with tensors B × L. Use only public histories, titles, descriptions, and timestamps; mark unavailable signals as unobserved. Preserve dataset routing, preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, and macro validation HR@10 for selection. Give five real training users per category full-catalog recommendations excluding seen items. Keep DATA_DIR sourced from os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'] and artifacts within the trial directory. Architecture changes must update the predictor writer.",
  "pseudocode": "DiagnosisProbe(view, device): retain model and compatibility interfaces\nrun_full_diagnosis(train_loader):\n  preserve model training state; enter evaluation mode\n  measure applicable probes without gradients using valid, nonpadding positions\n  aggregate measured values with explicit definitions and support counts\n  restore model training state\n  return {metrics, metric_definitions}\ndiagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis):\n  include measured metrics and their definitions\n  request evidence-based interpretation and distinguish observations from hypotheses\n  explicitly identify unavailable signals",
  "originality": {
    "score": 4,
    "positive": "Combines architecture-aware diagnostics with explicit observability constraints and a stable benchmark interface.",
    "negative": "The supplied description specifies an integration contract rather than a new diagnostic algorithm."
  },
  "future_potential": {
    "score": 7,
    "positive": "Could support repeatable diagnosis-driven model iteration across architectures and datasets.",
    "negative": "Its usefulness depends on the chosen probes and whether their recommendations improve validation HR@10; no results are provided."
  },
  "code_difficulty": {
    "score": 5,
    "positive": "Existing compatibility interfaces and a fixed batch format provide clear implementation boundaries.",
    "negative": "Architecture-specific probes, correct padding treatment, aggregation, and predictor synchronization require careful implementation. Higher scores indicate greater difficulty."
  }
}
